  "challenge": "Video at scale breaks on the edit. Every video needs hours of an editor's time for assembly, text overlays, transitions, and export \u2014 which means scaling output linearly scales expensive headcount. When a content program needs dozens of videos a week, that math doesn't work.",
  "approach": "I replaced the editing step with an API-driven pipeline. Templates define the structure (brand frames, transitions, text slots); source assets and AI-generated copy fill those slots through API calls to a video rendering service; the system handles captioning, audio sync, and platform-specific exports automatically. An editor is never opened. One brief produces multiple platform-native cuts in one run.",
  "result": "Video throughput increased 10x while per-video cost dropped sharply. The editing bottleneck simply doesn't exist anymore \u2014 videos are assembled programmatically, and scaling means running more jobs, not hiring more editors. One source asset now generates optimized outputs for every platform it needs to live on.",
